# =============================================================
# KAPIL OS — ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES (example)
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` for local development, and add the
# same variables as SECRETS in your deployment platform (Vercel,
# Netlify, etc.) under "Environment Variables".
#
# NEVER commit .env / .env.local. Never prefix secrets with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# Anything prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ is embedded in the client bundle and
# visible to every visitor — keep secrets server-side only.
# =============================================================

# ---- GitHub (optional) ---------------------------------------------
# Helps avoid GitHub API rate limits when the public API is saturated.
# Must be a PAT with only public read scopes (or none). Server-side ONLY.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=

# ---- Contact email delivery (optional) ------------------------------
# Delivered via the Resend REST API (no extra npm dependency).
# Get a key at https://resend.com
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# Verified sender you control (e.g. "Kapil OS <onboarding@resend.dev>",
# or "<no-reply@yourdomain.com>" after you verify a domain in Resend)
# CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL=
# Where messages go. In Resend test mode this must be the account owner's
# email; after verifying a domain it can be any address.
# CONTACT_TO_EMAIL=

# ---- Cloudflare Turnstile (optional) --------------------------------
# Invisible bot check for the contact form.
# Secret is server-side. The SITE KEY is public and may be prefixed
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ (that is its purpose).
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=

# ---- Deployment / SEO ----------------------------------------------
# The canonical origin used in metadata. Update before deploying.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://kapil-os.vercel.app
